findings.detail:
async function handleDeactivateConfirm(row: RosterRow): Promise<void> at :868-984.

Entry guard (:869): `if (deactivatePending) return;` — re-entrancy guard, same idiom as armDeactivate's own guard at :814.

:870-886 setup: captures `cfg = currentCfg` (bail if null), captures `activeAtStart`/`ownsFocus` for focus-restore bookkeeping, then sets `deactivatePending = true; deactivateRefusal = null; deactivateActionError = null;`.

try (:887-957):
  - resolves `dbEntityId` (throws if unresolvable, :897-900)
  - `libraryId = await resolveMyLibraryId(...)` (:912)
  - `blockers = await listDeactivateBlockers(...)` (:913)
  - refusal branch (:914-921): if blockers.length>0, sets `deactivateRefusal = { memberId: row.memberId, blockers }` and `return`s (deliberately does NOT clear `pendingDeactivateId` — comment at :915-918). No generation check on this branch.
  - success path (:922-957): `await deactivateMember(cfg, row.memberId);` then `pendingDeactivateId = null;` then `await loadForSelected();` (no generation check around either of these two lines or around `deactivateMember` itself). Then, only if `showInactive` is true, captures `const g = routeLoad.generation;` (:947, AFTER `loadForSelected()`, deliberately — comment :942-946) and reloads the inactive panel (:948-957) with `if (!routeLoad.isCurrent(g)) return;` guards inside both the success write (:951) and the catch (:954) of that inner try/catch.

catch (e) (:958-967): `console.error('roster: deactivate failed', row.memberId, e); deactivateActionError = { memberId: row.memberId, kind: 'deactivate' };` — `pendingDeactivateId` deliberately left set (comment :964-966). No generation check.

finally (:968-983):
```
finally {
    deactivatePending = false;
    // #286 — land focus back on the (now re-enabled) confirm for the two
    // outcomes that leave the pair mounted — refusal and failure — the
    // same landing `focusableByTestId` already gives `disarmRemove`/
    // `placeFocusAfterFailedRemove` (#273). Gated on `pendingDeactivateId`
    // still matching this row: on SUCCESS it is already null and the row
    // is on its way out via `loadForSelected()` above — a different shape
    // (async full-roster reload, not a local splice) with no same-render
    // neighbour to land on, so it is left untouched here, unchanged from
    // pre-#286 behaviour.
    if (ownsFocus && pendingDeactivateId === row.memberId) {
        await tick();
        focusableByTestId(`member-deactivate-confirm-${row.memberId}`)?.focus();
    }
}
```
`deactivatePending = false` is unconditional and carries NO generation check — this is the gap #287 names. The focus-restore line under it is gated on `pendingDeactivateId === row.memberId`, not on generation, so on a collective switch mid-flight (where `pendingDeactivateId` was reset to null by the route-load `reset` callback, :132) that particular DOM-focus side effect happens to be inert by coincidence of the id check, but `deactivatePending = false` itself always fires regardless of which collective is now selected.

Verified: the ONLY generation-guarded code inside handleDeactivateConfirm is the inner inactive-panel reload at :947-957:
```
const g = routeLoad.generation;
if (showInactive) {
    try {
        const rows = await loadInactiveRoster(cfg);
        if (!routeLoad.isCurrent(g)) return; // superseded — stale settle writes nothing
        inactiveRows = rows;
    } catch (e) {
        if (!routeLoad.isCurrent(g)) return;
        console.error('roster: inactive roster reload after deactivate failed', e);
    }
}
```
Generation capture: :947. Guard checks: :951 (success) and :954 (catch). Nothing else in the function — not the refusal branch, not the `deactivateMember`/`loadForSelected` success path, not the outer catch, not the finally — checks `routeLoad.isCurrent`. This matches the prior #273 research exactly; only the line numbers shifted (was ~877-886, now 947-957).

Introduced by commit 01ed068 (fix(#260)) in src/routes/profile/+page.svelte, then generalized into the shared route-load machine at src/lib/loading/routeLoad.ts. The machine keeps a private `generation` counter, bumped once per `loadForSelected()` call, exposed only as `readonly generation` (non-mutating getter) and `isCurrent(g: number): boolean` (`g === generation`) — see routeLoad.ts:76-83,150-158. The module's own doc comment (routeLoad.ts:16-19) names this pair as 'the EXTERNAL co-guard seam' for exactly this class of fix and explicitly calls out '#260's refreshCompletionGate and roster's several structural-write reconciles' as its intended reusers — i.e. this is not incidental overlap, the machine was built to be reused this way.

Canonical call shape, verbatim from src/routes/roster/+page.svelte:1647-1706 (performReparent's reconcile, one of many identical sites):
```
const g = routeLoad.generation;
...
try {
  await someAsyncWrite(...);
  if (g !== routeLoad.generation) return; // superseded by a newer collective selection
  ...write success state...
} catch (e) {
  ...
  if (g !== routeLoad.generation) return;
  ...
}
```
Equivalently written with the method form `if (!routeLoad.isCurrent(g)) return;` (e.g. roster/+page.svelte:951,954,1016,1019,1062,1065) — both forms compile to the same comparison; `isCurrent(g)` is just `g === generation` wrapped as a method. There is no other idiom in the codebase for this purpose.
